{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"ae4ff84df3042bb4","name":"card_unit_hurricane_mk_ii_c_trop","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/BrothersInArms/units/card_unit_hurricane_mk_ii_c_trop","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"HURRICANE Mk II-C TROP","text":"Becomes Veteran when it survives combat.","flavorText":"The Hurricane Mk II variant first saw service in 1940, with a more powerful engine and gradually improved armament. The Hurricane's main advantage over the Spitfire was that it was easier to fly, which was useful because squadrons were full of inexperienced pilots, and its gun platform was easier to handle than the Spitfire's. The unprotected fuel tank in front of the cockpit, on the other hand, could rupture and cause serious burn injuries to the pilot if hit. The wooden and fabric rear fuselages were also more prone to catching fire than metal fuselages. Despite its flaws, the Hurricane shot down the vast majority of enemy aircraft claimed by the RAF. The Hawker Hurricane and other aircraft were tropicalized, or \"trop\" for use in North Africa. They were given engine dust filters as well as a desert survival kit for the pilots.","faction":"Britain","type":"fighter","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":3,"operationCost":2,"attack":3,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_hurricane_mk_ii_c_trop","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_hurricane_mk_ii_c_trop_title","SourceString":"HURRICANE Mk II-C TROP","LocalizedString":"HURRICANE Mk II-C TROP"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":3,"defense":3,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_hurricane_mk_ii_c_trop_text","SourceString":"Becomes Veteran when it survives combat.","LocalizedString":"Becomes Veteran when it survives combat."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_hurricane_mk_ii_c_trop_history","SourceString":"The Hurricane Mk II variant first saw service in 